# Review packets / handoffs kept locally. Ignored because they are app-review working
# material that does not belong in a public repo — NOT because they hold secrets.
#
# CORRECTION: this comment, and the commit message on 97388e9, both used to claim these
# files "contain reviewer test credentials". They do not. Every credential-shaped item in
# all three is an env-var NAME followed by a blank; a scan for any 28+ character
# alphanumeric run returns zero hits, and the only Meta App ID present is public by design.
# The documents INSTRUCT a reader to create tester credentials; they contain none.
#
# This matters because the files remain reachable at 956332a, and the decision not to
# rewrite history was taken knowing exactly that. Do not reopen it believing credentials
# are sitting in the history — see docs/booking-open-decisions-research.md §3 for the
# verification and the full cost/benefit. The 97388e9 message cannot be corrected without
# the very rewrite that was declined, so this is where the record lives.
docs/Axentrio-App-Review-Submission-Packet.pdf
docs/meta-google-review-packet.md
docs/handoff-composable-templates-enablement.md

# Written by the deploy (ci.yml) so GET /health can report the running commit. NEVER committed:
# a checked-in value would ship a stale sha in every build, which is the exact lie the marker
# exists to prevent. See api/src/utils/build-info.ts.
api/public/commit.txt
